/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Length of training required in public sector jobs is high \(1\) meaning there will not be significant increases in labour supply when the wage rate increases because individuals are deterred from undertaking lengthy training \(1\) Specific qualifications are required to enter some public sector jobs such as teachers needing a degree \(1\) meaning there will not be significant increases in labour supply when the wage rate increases because individuals who are not already supplying their labour to the profession may not have the necessary qualifications to switch into the profession when the wage rate rises \(1\) Public sector jobs are vocational \(1\) meaning supply will not respond to a change in wage as individuals supply their labour because of job satisfaction rather than wage \(1\))
/E (Length of training required in public sector jobs is high \(1\) meaning there will not be significant increases in labour supply when the wage rate increases because individuals are deterred from undertaking lengthy training \(1\) Specific qualifications are required to enter some public sector jobs such as teachers needing a degree \(1\) meaning there will not be significant increases in labour supply when the wage rate increases because individuals who are not already supplying their labour to the profession may not have the necessary qualifications to switch into the profession when the wage rate rises \(1\) Public sector jobs are vocational \(1\) meaning supply will not respond to a change in wage as individuals supply their labour because of job satisfaction rather than wage \(1\))
